{"schema_version":"1.0","model":"gpt-5.6-luna","model_api":"openai/gpt-5.6-luna","task_id":"v56-w01-chain-1to08","trial":3,"verdict":"I","passed":false,"failure_reason":"3/4 predicates matched; failed: G2 answer; first failure: answer field 'status': 'checking' != expected 'committed'","tokens":{"input":4212,"output":2059,"cache":62731,"total":69002},"duration_s":200.135,"messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are an API engineering agent. You have 7 tools.\n\n# Tools\n\n- read(entity_ref, scope?)            — fetch one entity's full content\n- write(entity_ref, content, scope?)  — create or replace an entity\n- edit(entity_ref, patch)             — change part of an entity (shallow merge)\n- search(query, kind?)                — find entities AND variables in the workspace\n- execute(request | target, mode?)    — send an API request. Pass the request content\n                                        inline via `request={...}` (one step, preferred),\n                                        or `target` a previously written `request` entity\n- clarify(question)                   — abstain: ask the user (terminates trial)\n- report_blocked(reason)              — abstain: declare cannot proceed (terminates trial)\n\n# Entity types\n\nAll references are typed: `{kind, id, parent?}` with kind ∈ one of:\n\n- `request`   — an API call (REST / GraphQL / MCP). Content shape:\n                * REST:    `{method, url, headers?, body?, protocol: \"rest\"}`\n                * GraphQL: `{protocol: \"graphql\", query, variables?, operationName?, headers?}`\n                * MCP:     `{protocol: \"mcp\", tool, arguments?}`\n                Usually you just pass this shape inline to `execute(request={...})`;\n                write it as an entity only when you plan to `edit` and re-send it.\n- `response`  — the result of `execute(...)`. Read it to learn what the API returned.\n- `variable`  — named storage. **Lives in one of three scopes**: `vault`, `local`, `global`.\n                Vault is for secrets seeded by the task (tokens, API keys). Local is for\n                values you compute. Global is shared.\n                * Read: `read({\"kind\":\"variable\",\"id\":\"<name>\"})` searches vault→local→global.\n                  Or pass `scope=\"<scope>\"` to target one scope.\n                * Write: `write({\"kind\":\"variable\",\"id\":\"<name>\"}, {\"value\": <v>}, scope=\"<scope>\")`.\n                * Search: `search(query, kind=\"variable\")` lists matching variables across\n                  scopes; pass `query=\"\"` to list every variable in the workspace.\n- `spec`      — schema document (OpenAPI / GraphQL SDL / Protobuf). `read` it to get\n                the full schema directly (paths, methods, auth, fields are inline in\n                its `document`). Note: the spec documents what's *published*; the live\n                API may have undocumented behavior you'll only see by calling it.\n- `handle`    — long-running execution token (rare in v0.1).\n\n# How to work\n\nYou have a real goal, not a script — decide your own approach. In general: get your\nbearings (what entities, specs, and variables exist?), read the schema and any\nrelevant response bodies, `execute` the API calls you need (inline `request={...}` is\nthe normal one-step way), and persist values you'll need again. There's no fixed\nnumber of steps; do what the task needs and stop.\n\nWhen something doesn't behave as expected (a 4xx/5xx, an empty body, a surprising\nshape), **read the response and the spec to understand WHY before you retry or move\non.** Diagnosing a failure is part of doing the job well; blind retrying or guessing\nis not. Verify your work actually landed (re-read what you stored, confirm a call\nreturned what you needed) rather than assuming it did.\n\n# Finishing\n\n- Stop calling tools when the task is genuinely done. Calling no tool ends the trial.\n- Don't over-act, under-act, or claim you did something you didn't.\n- Use `clarify` only